# (1.4.1) PRESETS spun fast, playing: each click sends a whole piece to the engine, which takes one over ~7 blocks, so
# four clicks or more filled its queue and the piece arrived at lost its last commands, playing partly as the pieces
# passed through while the screen showed its own (the 1.4.0 shorts' takes: Concrete's LFO at Fog's 32 bars). The UI
# now sends the piece again once the queue has room: the engine and the screen agree
listen
wait 3000
expect endiff 0
turn PRESET 4 5
wait 3000
expect piece 4
expect qdrops >0
expect endiff 0
turn PRESET 3 5
wait 3000
expect piece 7
expect endiff 0
turn PRESET -7 5
wait 3000
expect piece 0
expect endiff 0
turn PRESET 1 400
wait 2000
expect piece 1
expect endiff 0
